// Regression case for commit fc46e9db: an underscore-separated `\u{...}`
// escape must decode to the same value Cedar (and Rust) give it.
//
// Cedar delegates to Rust's string-escape grammar, which permits `_` digit
// separators inside `\u{...}`: `"\u{4_1}"` decodes to the single character `A`
// (0x41). The pre-fix decode_string parsed the braced body with
// `u32::from_str_radix(hex, 16)`, which does NOT accept underscores, so it
// silently fell through to its "malformed" branch and passed the literal
// through verbatim as the six characters `\`, `u`, `{`, `4`, `_`, `1`, `}`.
//
// This is the insidious facet — not a rejection but a WRONG VALUE. The guard
// `context.input.document == "\u{4_1}"` should match a real document == "A"
// event (verdict true); on the buggy prefix it never matches (verdict false).
permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Read",
    resource
)
when { context.input.document == "\u{4_1}" };
